          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Trigonometric Ratios of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 5 ^ { \\circ }"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.164,
            0.594,
            0.222
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta   \\mathrm { A B C } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " right-angled at B, if one angle is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 5 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , then the other angle is also "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 5 ^ { \\circ } , \\mathrm { i . e . } , \\angle \\mathrm { A } = \\angle \\mathrm { C } = 4 5 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (see Fig. 8.14)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.228,
            0.135,
            0.245
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.292,
            0.227,
            0.51,
            0.247
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{BC} = \\mathrm{AB} \\quad (\\mathrm{Why?})"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.713,
            0.137,
            0.893,
            0.257
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.713,
                0.137,
                0.893,
                0.257
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_9_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.253,
            0.384,
            0.272
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, Suppose "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{BC} = \\mathrm{AB} = a."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.759,
            0.263,
            0.858,
            0.282
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fig. 8.14"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.278,
            0.726,
            0.297
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Then by Pythagoras Theorem, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "AC^{2} = AB^{2} + BC^{2} = a^{2} + a^{2} = 2a^{2}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.309,
            0.417,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "and, therefore, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { A C } =   a { \\sqrt { 2 } }   ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.341,
            0.653,
            0.36
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Using the definitions of the trigonometric ratios, we have :"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.373,
            0.736,
            0.418
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "\\sin 45^{\\circ} = \\frac{ side opposite to angle   45^{\\circ}}{ hyponeuse } = \\frac{BC}{AC} = \\frac{a}{a\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.181,
            0.435,
            0.735,
            0.481
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "\\cos 45^{\\circ} = \\frac{\\overline{ side adjacent to angle 45^{\\circ}}}{\\overline{ hypotenuse }} = \\frac{\\overline{AB}}{\\overline{AC}} = \\frac{a}{a\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.185,
            0.498,
            0.682,
            0.543
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "\\tan 45^{\\circ} = \\frac{\\overline{side opposite to angle 45^{\\circ}}}{\\overline{side adjacent to angle 45^{\\circ}}} = \\frac{\\overline{BC}}{\\overline{AB}} = \\frac{a}{a} = 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.563,
            0.896,
            0.605
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Also, cosec "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "45^{\\circ} = \\frac{1}{\\sin 45^{\\circ}} = \\sqrt{2}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , sec "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "45^{\\circ} = \\frac{1}{\\cos 45^{\\circ}} = \\sqrt{2}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , cot "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 5 ^ { \\circ } = { \\frac { 1 } { \\tan   4 5 ^ { \\circ } } }   =   1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.624,
            0.485,
            0.644
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Trigonometric Ratios of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { 3 0 ^ { \\circ } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { 6 0 ^ { \\circ } }"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.65,
            0.595,
            0.727
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us now calculate the trigonometric ratios of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Consider an equilateral triangle ABC. Since each angle in an equilateral triangle is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , therefore, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{A} = \\angle \\mathrm{B} = \\angle \\mathrm{C} = 60^{\\circ}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.733,
            0.593,
            0.771
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Draw the perpendicular AD from A to the side BC (see Fig. 8.15)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
